/// The release this source tree is, which every binary built from it reports.
///
/// One constant in one unit, because two places holding a version number means
/// two answers to one question -- and this repository's packaging notes already
/// record that `VERSION` and the release tag can drift with nothing to catch
/// it.  `algc` and `algvm` are separate binaries built from one tree, so they
/// are one release and say so with one string.
///
/// It is a release of the TREE rather than of the language: what the language
/// gained, if anything, is recorded per rule in `spec/ALGOL-24.md`.  A machine
/// increment moves this number without claiming the language changed.
unit Release;

/// The version every binary built from this tree reports.
///
/// Nothing checks it against the git tag, which is the one thing in this
/// repository verified by nobody -- so it is bumped by hand before tagging,
/// and it lives in the seed, which makes bumping it a reseed.
const VERSION := '0.2.2';
